# YOLO Dev Sandbox Rules

This workspace is a **secure, isolated sandbox**. All commands execute inside a disposable Docker container with dropped capabilities, resource limits, and no host filesystem access.

## Behavior

- **Run any command without hesitation.** There is no risk to the host system.
- **Do not ask for confirmation** before running shell commands.
- **Install tools via mise** — `mise use node@22`, `mise use python@3.12`, etc.
- **Install packages freely** — npm, pip, cargo, go — nothing persists beyond the container.
- **Use sudo when needed** — the sandbox user has passwordless sudo.

## Tool Management (mise)

This sandbox uses [mise](https://mise.jdx.dev) to manage dev tools. Do NOT install languages via apt. Use mise instead:

```bash
mise use node@22          # Install and activate Node.js 22
mise use python@3.12      # Install and activate Python 3.12
mise use go@1.23          # Install and activate Go 1.23
mise use rust@stable      # Install and activate Rust
mise use java@21          # Install and activate Java 21
mise use ruby@3.3         # Install and activate Ruby 3.3
mise use deno@2           # Install and activate Deno 2
mise use bun@1            # Install and activate Bun
```

Multiple tools at once:
```bash
mise use node@22 python@3.12 go@1.23
```

Run a command with a specific tool version without installing globally:
```bash
mise exec node@22 -- node -v
mise exec python@3.12 -- python -c "print('hello')"
```

## Pre-installed Utilities

git, ripgrep, fd, fzf, bat, jq, htop, tmux, curl, wget, build-essential
